[01:17.46] When all is withered and torn,
[01:21.85] And all has perished and fallen,
[01:26.19] These great wooden doors shall remain closed. . .
[01:36.02] When the heart is a grave filled with blood,
[01:45.86] And the soul is a cold and haunted shall of lost hope.
[02:12.48] When the voice of pride has been silenced,
[02:16.96] And dignity's fires are but cinders,
[02:21.56] . . .their grandeur shall remain untainted.
[03:29.20] It is this grandeur that protects the spirit within,
[03:38.37] From the plight of this broken world, from the wounds in her song.
[04:24.83] I wish to die with my will and spirit intact,
[04:30.20] The will that inspired me to write these words.
[04:34.78] Seek not the fallen to unlock these wooden doors.
[04:49.65] 